From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:43:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Move a playlist entry by its id in core

The apps built a playlist's whole new order from the rows they had
loaded and wrote it. Now a move names the entry's position id and the
place it lands, and core renumbers the entries in one SQL write, which
fails when the playlist no longer holds the entry. Each entry row says
whether an entry comes before and after it, and Android offers its
screen reader moves from those instead of searching the loaded rows.
Each app's drag holds the dragged entry itself rather than finding it
by index.

